---
title: The WhereTo Trips Partner Program — Texas Partner Pilot
description: You bring the audience, we share the revenue. Earn 30% of what WhereTo Trips makes on every trip your audience books, for three years after they sign up with your link.
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/TexasPartners/"
---
{#- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Texas Partner Pilot — the creator info sheet as a page of this site.

    Built from the site's own sections rather than as a port of the PDF
    (WhereTo_Partner_InfoSheet_Combined.pdf, Sep 2026): hero-slider,
    highlights, feature-split, tile, stat-row, step-card, download-band.
    They carry this site's mobile behaviour already — the hero in
    particular restacks into photo-band-then-copy below 720px, which a
    hand-rolled two-column sheet layout does not.

    Mobile first: every rule here is written for the narrow case and
    widened with min-width queries, because most creators will open this
    from a link in a message.

    Numbers come from engineStats.json and appModes.json, not from the
    PDF — /destinations and /how-it-works quote the same data files, and
    a partner page that says 900 next to a site that says 1,000+ reads
    as one of them being wrong.
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}

{%- set mailto = "mailto:Chris@WhereToTrips.com?subject=Texas%20Partner%20Pilot" -%}
{%- set heroImg = "https://pvqwxphrmcvmztlkzhsg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/destination-stock-images/whereto-explore-dashboard/a-team-of-travelers-looking-at-the-lake-in-austria-2026-03-19-10-13-37-utc.jpg" -%}

{#- The sheet's order for the four workflows, which is not appModes.json's.
    Both data files are looked up by key with an inline loop: Nunjucks scopes
    `set` to the loop body, so a match cannot be hoisted out to a variable,
    and `selectattr` here returns the whole list instead of filtering it. -#}
{%- set modeOrder = ["discover", "explore", "together", "direct"] -%}

<style>
  /* ═════ Texas Partner Pilot ═════════════════════════════════════════
     Page-scoped. This is one outreach page's layout, not a section type
     anything else composes from, so it does not belong in styles.css
     where every other page would download it.

     Written narrow-first; min-width queries widen it. Overrides of
     shared classes (.highlights, .step-card) are class-on-class, which
     outranks styles.css's own max-width queries — so every responsive
     step those classes need is restated here rather than inherited. */

  /* ── Offer bar over the hero ──────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-hl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text h4 {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 34px; color: var(--amber);
    line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text h4 .tp-unit {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 3px;
  }
  .tp-hl .highlight-text p { font-size: 13.5px; }

  /* ── Hero, wide screens only ──────────────────────────────────────────
     Every rule here is inside min-width:721px on purpose. This <style>
     block comes after styles.css, so an unscoped .hero-slider or
     .slide-caption h1 rule would also beat the shared max-width:720px
     mobile rules and undo the stacked phone hero. */
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    /* The home page's full-viewport hero is a front door. This is a page
       someone was sent to read, so it opens shorter. */
    .hero-slider { height: clamp(520px, 74vh, 700px); }
    /* Wide enough that each sentence of the headline holds one line. */
    .slide-caption { max-width: 880px; }
    .slide-caption h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 5.2vw, 64px); }
    .sec-head { max-width: 820px; }
    /* The shared wash clears by 68% of the width. This page's headline runs
       wider than the home page's, so it carries further before fading. */
    .hero-slide-overlay {
      background:
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(25,25,25,0.76) 0%, rgba(25,25,25,0.56) 42%,
                               rgba(25,25,25,0.24) 64%, rgba(25,25,25,0) 78%),
        linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(25,25,25,0.5) 0%, transparent 45%);
    }
  }

  /* The shared rule caps the photo-overlaid eyebrow at 70% of the width,
     which wraps this page's longer one and strands the separator. */
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .slide-eyebrow { max-width: 94%; } }

  /* ── Vibe Engine: the worked example ──────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-example { margin-top: 28px; }
  .tp-example-label {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted);
    display: block; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .tp-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .tp-chip-result {
    background: var(--amber-tint); border-color: var(--amber);
    color: var(--amber-deep); font-weight: 600; cursor: default;
  }
  .tp-chip-result:hover {
    background: var(--amber); color: #fff; border-color: var(--amber);
  }
  .tp-chip-budget { background: var(--azure-tint); border-color: var(--azure); color: var(--azure); font-weight: 700; }

  .feature-img.tp-phone { height: clamp(220px, 46vw, 300px); }
  @media (min-width: 961px) { .feature-img.tp-phone { height: clamp(300px, 30vw, 420px); } }

  /* ── Card grids ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-ways { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px; }
  .tp-ways .tile { padding: 12px 12px 18px; }
  .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 104px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .tp-ways h3 { font-size: 17px; }
  .tp-ways p { font-size: 13px; }

  .tp-benefits { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .tp-benefit-num {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 30px;
    color: var(--azure); line-height: 1; display: block; margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  /* ── Where the money sits ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-money { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 26px; align-items: center; }
  /* On a phone the two rates are the headline, so they lead. */
  .tp-money-figs {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0; order: -1;
    background: var(--tint); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 26px 16px;
  }
  .tp-money-fig { text-align: center; padding: 6px 12px; }
  .tp-money-fig + .tp-money-fig { border-left: 1px solid var(--wg300); }
  .tp-money-fig .tp-num {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(34px, 9vw, 54px);
    color: var(--amber); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .tp-money-fig .tp-unit { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--amber); }
  .tp-money-fig p { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .tp-soon {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .tp-soon .chip { opacity: .75; }
  .tp-soon .chip:hover { background: var(--card); color: var(--navy); border-color: var(--wg200); transform: none; box-shadow: none; }
  .tp-soon-label {
    display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 10px; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* ── Follower pull-quote ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-quote {
    background: var(--footer); border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: clamp(34px, 7vw, 60px) clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px); text-align: center;
    background-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at 22% 30%, rgba(32,156,224,0.22) 0%, transparent 62%),
                      radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 70%, rgba(230,152,0,0.14) 0%, transparent 62%);
  }
  .tp-quote .eyebrow { color: var(--amber); }
  .tp-quote h2 {
    color: #fff; font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(27px, 6vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.16; margin: 6px auto 16px; max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .tp-quote p {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.76); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 48ch; margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* ── Five steps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .tp-note {
    margin-top: 22px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* ── Closing CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .tp-mail-btn { font-size: 15px; text-transform: none; }
  .tp-fine {
    margin: 30px auto 0; max-width: 62ch; text-align: left;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--amber); padding-left: 16px;
  }
  .tp-fine h4 {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--amber);
    letter-spacing: .04em; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .tp-fine p { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.68); margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .tp-legal {
    font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 96ch; margin: 26px auto 0; text-align: center;
  }

  /* ── Sticky reply bar, phones only ────────────────────────────────────
     The page is long and the one action it asks for sits at the bottom of
     it. The bar appears once the hero has scrolled away and hides again
     over the closing CTA so it never covers the address it duplicates. */
  .tp-bar {
    position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 60;
    padding: 10px 16px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.96); backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--wg200); box-shadow: 0 -6px 24px rgba(20,30,40,0.10);
    transform: translateY(110%); transition: transform .28s ease;
  }
  .tp-bar.is-on { transform: none; }
  .tp-bar .btn { width: 100%; justify-content: center; padding: 15px 20px; }
  @media (min-width: 721px) { .tp-bar { display: none; } }

  /* ── Wider screens ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (min-width: 561px) {
    .tp-benefits { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
    .tp-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
    .tp-ways { gap: 18px; }
    .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 140px; }
    .tp-money-fig p { font-size: 14px; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 721px) {
    .tp-hl { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .tp-hl .highlight-text h4 { font-size: 38px; }
    .tp-money { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .tp-money-figs { order: 0; }
    .tp-soon { justify-content: flex-start; }
    .tp-soon-label { text-align: left; }
    .tp-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (min-width: 961px) {
    .tp-ways { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 22px; }
    .tp-ways .tile-img { height: 150px; }
    .tp-ways h3 { font-size: 20px; }
    .tp-ways p { font-size: 13.5px; }
    .tp-benefits { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
    .tp-steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
    .tp-steps .step-card { padding: 24px 20px; }
  }
</style>

{# ═══ Hero ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="hero-slider">
  <div class="hero-slides">
    <div class="hero-slide active" role="img"
         aria-label="Two travelers on a rock above a mountain lake, one pointing across the water"
         style="background-image:url('{{ heroImg | thumb(1800, 75) }}')"></div>
    <div class="hero-slide-overlay"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap hero-caption-wrap">
    <div class="slide-caption">
      <div class="slide-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow">Texas Partner Pilot &middot; October 2026</span></div>
      <div class="slide-title">
        <h1>You bring the audience.
<span class="italic">We share the revenue.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="slide-subtitle">
        <p class="lede">Your audience already comes to you for where to go next. Share WhereTo Trips
          with them the way you share everything else, and you earn 30% of what we make on every
          trip they book, for three years after they sign up with your link.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="btns">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#apply">Apply to the pilot</a>
        <a class="btn btn-hero-ghost" href="#what-you-earn">See what you earn</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ The offer, in three numbers ═══════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="highlights-wrap">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="highlights tp-hl reveal">
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "hand-money" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>30<span class="tp-unit">%</span></h4>
          <p>Of our revenue, shared with you on every completed booking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "calendar" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>3<span class="tp-unit">years</span></h4>
          <p>Per traveler, on every trip they complete. Recurring, not one-off.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="highlight">
        <span class="highlight-icon">{% icon "camera" %}</span>
        <div class="highlight-text">
          <h4>4<span class="tp-unit">posts</span></h4>
          <p>A year is all we ask. The more you promote, the more you earn.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ Who we are ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="feature-split">
      <div class="feature-img-wrap reveal">
        <img class="feature-img" src="/media/partners/texas-partner-hero-720.jpg"
             srcset="/media/partners/texas-partner-hero-720.jpg 720w, /media/partners/texas-partner-hero.jpg 1200w"
             sizes="(max-width: 960px) 92vw, 46vw"
             alt="A traveler looking out over a mountain lake" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="feature-text reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <span class="eyebrow">Start with you</span>
        <h2>End up somewhere <span class="italic">amazing.</span></h2>
        <p class="lede">WhereTo Trips is a Texas based travel technology platform. We help people
          figure out where to go, plan the trip, and book it in one place.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">We are launching in Texas first, with a small roster of creators whose
          audiences already come to them for travel advice. That is the whole pilot: a handful of
          people who are already trusted, sharing something worth being trusted with.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ The Vibe Engine ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block tint" id="vibe-engine">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="feature-split flip">
      <div class="feature-img-wrap reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <img class="feature-img img-transparent tp-phone" src="/media/oniPhone_2.png"
             alt="The WhereTo app showing a scored destination result" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <div class="feature-text reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Vibe Engine</span>
        <h2>Where will your vibes <span class="italic">take you?</span></h2>
        <p class="lede">WhereTo is the only travel app on the map that is truly interested in the
          traveler and what they want to experience.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">A traveler gives us a budget, dates and the vibes they are after, and
          the Vibe Engine returns destinations that fit, with a flight and hotel package at or under
          that budget.</p>

        <div class="tp-example">
          <span class="tp-example-label">What a traveler puts in</span>
          <div class="tp-chips">
            <span class="chip tp-chip-budget">$3,400</span>
            <span class="chip">A week in March</span>
            <span class="chip">Food &amp; live music</span>
            <span class="chip">Beach &amp; boardwalk</span>
            <span class="chip">Coastal &amp; sea fishing</span>
            <span class="chip">Escape to an island</span>
            <span class="chip">Family Friendly</span>
          </div>
          <span class="tp-example-label" style="margin-top: 18px;">What comes back, scored</span>
          <div class="tp-chips">
            <span class="chip tp-chip-result">Cabo San Lucas, MX &middot; 92</span>
            <span class="chip tp-chip-result">Newquay, UK &middot; 87</span>
            <span class="chip tp-chip-result">Valparaiso, FL &middot; 93</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-row reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-top: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);">
      {%- for st in engineStats.stats -%}
        {%- if st.key == "vibes" or st.key == "destinations" %}
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-num">{{ st.display }}</span>
        <span class="stat-label">{{ st.label }}</span>
      </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor %}
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-num">{{ appModes | length }}</span>
        <span class="stat-label">ways in, one engine behind them</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ Four ways your audience finds a trip ══════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block" id="four-ways">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Four ways in</span>
      <h2>However they start, they <span class="italic">end up booking.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">Flights and hotels are bookable at launch. Cars, insurance and excursions are
        planned, and your share covers those too when they land.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tp-ways reveal reveal-delay-1">
      {% for key in modeOrder %}{% for m in appModes %}{% if m.key == key %}
      {#- New tab: this is an outreach page someone was sent, and a workflow
          page is a detour off it rather than the next step. Losing their
          place on the way back is how they stop reading it. -#}
      <a class="tile" href="{{ m.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img class="tile-img" src="{{ m.images[0] | thumb(520) }}"
             srcset="{{ m.images[0] | thumbSet([320, 520, 760]) }}"
             sizes="(max-width: 960px) 46vw, 23vw"
             alt="{{ m.title }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <h3>{% if m.key == "together" %}Wander Together{% else %}{{ m.titleAccent }}{% endif %}</h3>
        <p>{{ m.short }}.</p>
      </a>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ What's in it for you ══════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block tint" id="what-you-earn">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's in it for you</span>
      <h2>New ongoing revenue from <span class="italic">the audience you already have.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tp-benefits reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">1</span>
        <h3>30% of what we earn</h3>
        <p>A supplier pays us a commission on the trip. 30% of that commission is yours, on every
          completed booking. No rates to negotiate and no invoices to send.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">2</span>
        <h3>Three years, per traveler</h3>
        <p>The clock starts the day they download the app and register, not the day they book. All
          bookings they make for 3 years you share in the revenue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">3</span>
        <h3>Your voice, your content</h3>
        <p>People follow you for the way you travel and the way you tell it. Keep doing exactly that,
          and talk about WhereTo in your own words. We never write your script or edit your opinion.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">4</span>
        <h3>A live partner dashboard</h3>
        <p>Sign in at WhereToTrips.com to see downloads, registrations, bookings and estimated
          revenue share.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">5</span>
        <h3>Results for all posted content</h3>
        <p>We track the performance of each post, blog, newsletter and campaign with a unique link
          and promo code, giving you a clear view of what's driving results and what's not.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <span class="tp-benefit-num">6</span>
        <h3>Paid monthly by ACH</h3>
        <p>Paid once travel is completed, with a $50 minimum that rolls forward. W-9 and ACH
          authorization are collected at onboarding.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ Where the money sits ══════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tp-money">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Where the money sits</span>
        <h2 style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; margin: 6px 0 18px;">
          The stay is where <span class="italic">the revenue is.</span></h2>
        <p class="body-copy">A booking heavy on accommodation pays you considerably more than one
          that is mostly airfare. New components are pure upside: your 30% covers what we earn, not
          a fixed product list.</p>
        <div class="tp-soon">
          <span class="chip">Rental cars</span>
          <span class="chip">Excursions</span>
          <span class="chip">Travel insurance</span>
        </div>
        <span class="tp-soon-label">Coming soon, and covered by the same 30%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tp-money-figs reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="tp-money-fig">
          <span class="tp-num">15-30</span><span class="tp-unit">%</span>
          <p>revenue on hotels</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tp-money-fig">
          <span class="tp-num">0-1</span><span class="tp-unit">%</span>
          <p>revenue on flights</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ What your followers get ═══════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tp-quote reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What is in it for your followers?</span>
      <h2>What if your next trip found you?</h2>
      <p>Somewhere they would never have searched for, inside the budget they actually had. A week
        they will still talk about years later, and they will remember who sent them there.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ═══ How to get started ════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block tint" id="get-started">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">How to get started</span>
      <h2>Up and running <span class="italic">in five steps.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tp-steps reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <h3>Have a short call</h3>
        <p>Reply and we will set one up. A short conversation about fit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <h3>Sign on</h3>
        <p>Partner Agreement and Program Terms, plus W-9 and ACH, all in Zoho Sign.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <h3>Get your dashboard</h3>
