{# ═══ Apply ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   The same form /partners/ uses, by including the same partial
   rather than copying its markup, so a change to partner_application.njk
   reaches both pages at once. Both write into Zoho CRM Leads through
   capture-submission; only the email subject names the pilot, so Chris can
   tell them apart in an inbox.
   The sticky reply bar hides from here down (data-tp-cta), because from
   here on the thing it links to is already on screen.
   `background` is off only because the steps section above it is tinted;
   two tinted blocks in a row run together as one. #}
{%- set s = {
  "eyebrow": "Become a creator partner",
  "title": { "pre": "Let's make something", "accent": "together", "post": "." },
  "id": "apply",
  "background": false,
  "body": "Tell us about your audience and what you cover. We'll be in touch about partnering.",
  "subject": "Texas Partner Pilot application — WhereTo",
  "buttonLabel": "Apply to become a partner"
} -%}
<div data-tp-cta>
  {% include "sections/partner_application.njk" %}
</div>

{# ═══ Closing CTA ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="block" id="or-email">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="download-band reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions? Email me directly</span>
      <h2>Let's talk about <span class="italic">your audience.</span></h2>
