          posts a year, prorated in year one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="tp-legal">VC Innovations Group LLC d/b/a WhereTo Trips. This page describes the
      WhereTo Trips Partner Program in general terms. The Partner Agreement and Program Terms and
      Conditions govern the relationship and control in the event of any inconsistency. Earnings
      depend on traveler bookings and are not guaranteed; nothing here is a projection of what any
      partner will earn. Features described as planned are not currently available.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# Sticky reply bar — phones only, and never over the CTA it duplicates. #}
<div class="tp-bar" id="tp-bar">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#apply">Apply to the pilot</a>
</div>
<script>
  (function () {
    var bar = document.getElementById('tp-bar');
    var hero = document.querySelector('.hero-slider');
    var cta = document.querySelector('[data-tp-cta]');
    if (!bar || !hero || !cta) return;
    // A scroll listener rather than an IntersectionObserver: same behaviour,
    // and its state can actually be asserted from a headless run, where IO
    // delivery is suppressed.
    var heroBottom = 0;
    function measure() {
      heroBottom = hero.getBoundingClientRect().bottom + window.scrollY;
      sync();
    }
    function sync() {
      var past = window.scrollY > heroBottom - 40;
      // Once the closing CTA comes into view the bar stays down for the
      // rest of the page, rather than popping back up over the footer.
      var reachedCta = cta.getBoundingClientRect().top < window.innerHeight;
      bar.classList.toggle('is-on', past && !reachedCta);
    }
    measure();
    window.addEventListener('load', measure);
    window.addEventListener('resize', measure);
    window.addEventListener('scroll', sync, { passive: true });
  })();
</script>
